<<<
choliambic (Pros.); *‘ lame iambic °. A classical metre changed from the ordinary iambic (see below) by having always a spondee in the sixth & an iambus in the fifth foot: O quid /sélit /is ést /béat /itis/ctiris? Also called scazon.
===
*choliambic* (Pros.); ‘lame iambic’. A classical metre changed from the ordinary *iambic* (see below) by having always a spondee in the sixth & an iambus in the fifth foot: Ō quīd/sŏlūt/īs ēst/bĕāt/iūs/cūrīs? Also called *scazon*.
>>>

